                                      else on file covers: defining only
                                      column 1 gets a 130 byte row
                                      carrying just "1", defining only
                                      column 3 gets "varchar1" in slot 3,
                                      and the undefined columns
                                      contribute no bytes at all.  the
                                      row header's count is the number of
                                      real defines, not the number of
                                      descriptors the request names -
                                      -defines3 names three and its row
                                      header says 1 (#9810)
    9810-redhat9x86-portable-midfetch-defines3-sqlrelay.oraproxy
                                     the --defines=3 run again, against
                                      sqlrelay's oracleprotocoloci7
                                      instance instead of the real
                                      server, so the same client's
                                      request appears in the portable
                                      encoding - the only one this module
                                      ever negotiates (#9812), and so the
                                      only one its define parse has to
                                      read.  its row is the bug itself:
                                      sqlrelay answering a one-column
                                      define with all four columns, which
                                      is what segfaulted the real client.
                                      pair it with the native
                                      -defines3-realserver capture above
