                                      sequence.  note a run that defines
                                      every column did not crash, which
                                      is why this went unnoticed for so
                                      long (#9810)
    9976-redhat9x86-portable-midfetch-defines1-sqlrelay.oraproxy
                                     the --defines=1 run against
                                      sqlrelay, taken after the #9976 fix
                                      - the sqlrelay side of the
                                      -defines1-realserver capture above,
                                      which nothing on file had until
                                      then.  it holds a legacy fetch run
                                      to exhaustion, which is what #9702
                                      spent four comments unable to get:
                                      three fetch answers whose
                                      rows-processed field counts 1, 2, 3
                                      rather than repeating the per-call
                                      count, and then a past-the-end
                                      answer that is the ordinary summary
                                      object carrying 1403 with
                                      "ORA-01403: no data found" and its
